          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: rabugento",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rabugento — \"grumpy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "De manhã, antes do café, sou rabugento. In the morning, before coffee, I am grumpy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Informal. Ser rabugento is a trait; estar rabugento is a mood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rabugento is built on rabugem \"mange in dogs\" (EtymDB), which goes back to Latin rōbīgō \"rust, blight\" (Lewis & Short): a grumpy person is as touchy as a dog with mange."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
